    "result_text": "All tests pass. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## What I implemented\n\n`customerCode` formatted `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` is now assigned at owner creation and returned on reads.\n\n**Format logic** \u2014 a new single-responsibility function step, mirroring the existing `DefaultOwnerRegistrationDate`:\n- `rest/function/owner/AssignOwnerCustomerCode.java` \u2014 builds `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` where LAST3 is the upper-cased first three letters of `lastName` and NNNN is `%04d` of `ownerRepository.findAll().size() + 1` (one more than the current owner count), then sets it in place on the built entity.\n\n**Pipeline wiring** \u2014 `officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`: inserted `assignCustomerCode` between `defaultRegistrationDate` and `save`, under `govern: [ transaction ]` so the count read and the write share one transaction (keeping the global sequence consistent).\n\n**Model & persistence**:\n- `model/Owner.java` \u2014 added `customerCode` field (`@Column(name = \"customer_code\")`) with getter/setter.\n- `db/{hsqldb,h2,postgres,mysql}/schema.sql` \u2014 added the `customer_code` column.\n\n**API contract** \u2014 `openapi.yml`: added `customerCode` as a `readOnly` property on the `Owner` schema (alongside `displayName`/`initials`), so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct maps it by name automatically (no mapper change needed).\n\n## Verification\n- `AcceptanceTest.coreFormatAndGlobalSequence` passes: `SMI-`/`JON-` prefixes and the global sequence (`cb == ca + 1`) both hold.\n- Full test suite: **BUILD SUCCESS**, 0 failures.\n\nBecause the code is assigned only in the POST pipeline, the PUT flow (`ApplyOwner`, which mutates only editable fields) leaves an existing `customerCode` untouched.",
